   <text type="letter">
      <body>
         <div type="writingSession">
            <pb n="1"/>
            <opener><dateline><date when="1934-05-21">May 21, 1934</date></dateline>
               <salute>My dear <rs ref="#tillich_person_id__1928" type="person">Professor
                     Tillich</rs></salute>
            </opener>
            <p>On behalf of the Board of Directors, may I extend to you a very cordial invitation to
               deliver two courses in the first semester in the academic year 1934-1935 in the
               sphere of the philosophy of religion and systematic theology.</p>
            <p>We have greatly appreciated the service you have rendered this year and are confident
               that with greater familiarity with English you will find yourself making an even
               larger contribution to our students in the coming year.</p>
            <closer><salute>Faithfully yours,</salute>
               <signed>President <rs ref="#tillich_person_id__386" type="person">Henry S.
                     Coffin</rs></signed>
            </closer>
         </div>
      </body>
   </text>
